---
title: Sticky Chinese five-spice chicken traybake
servings: 4
course: dinner
cuisine: Chinese
tags: chicken, baked, one-pan
image: https://images.immediate.co.uk/production/volatile/sites/30/2020/08/sticky-chinese-chicken-traybake-f28c3b7.jpg?resize=440,400
source: https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/sticky-chinese-chicken-traybake
prep time: 10m
cook time: 40m
---

Heat the #oven{} to 200 C. Arrange the @chicken thigh{8}(skin on and bone in, slashed 2-3 times) in a #baking tray{}.

Mix together the @hoisin sauce{4%tbsp}, @sesame oil{2%tsp}, @honey{2%tbsp}(clear), @chinese five-spice powder{1.5%tsp}, @ginger{15%g}(grated), @garlic clove{2}(grated) and some @-salt{}(to season) and @-black pepper{}(to season) in a #bowl{}.

Pour over the @&chicken thigh{} and toss to coat -- you could now marinate for ~{2%hours} if you have time.

Roast, skin-side up, in the #oven{} for ~{35%minutes}, basting at least once.

Stir through the @cashew nut{50%g}(toasted) and sprinkle the @spring onion{4}(chopped) over the chicken. Return to the #oven{} for ~{5%minutes}, then serve with @brown rice{400%g}(cooked).
